WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.680
OpenAI is sharing its full defense factory architecture so any team can run continuous ai agent loops that find, validate, and fix vulnerabilities across hundreds of systems. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 169. The effort mobilized 250 people and used the company's latest cyber models. OpenAI released the full architecture along with a practical implementation guide that other organizations can follow directly. The loop runs agents that locate

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:45.280
problems, test whether each one is real, and verify that patches eliminate them without introducing new weaknesses. Teams working on large-scale infrastructure or security tooling now have a concrete reference for deploying the same agent-driven vulnerability management.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:01:09.840
StockBench introduces a lean 4-bench mark with 450 graduate-level stochastic processes problems drawn from finite and countable Markov chains, renewal processes, random walks, martingales, stopping times, cues, brownie in motion, stochastic calculus, weak convergence, and plason processes. Each problem is paired with its natural language source.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:20.780
An Opus 4.8-based agent achieved a 34.9% proof rate, 157 out of 450, under a 15-minute-per-problem limit.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:30.760
Osprey bootstraps speculative decoding drafters from off-the-shelf pre-trained small-language models rather than training them from scratch against a single target.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:49.580
A single pre-trained backbone transfers across targets and improves mean acceptance length by 16.1% for Quinn-38B, 21.2% for Lama-3.370B Instruct, and 22.7% for the 229B Minimax M2.5.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:57.820
The method delivers 17.5% higher tokens per second with the largest gains on out-of-domain and multilingual data.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:15.980
Buzz ASR releases 102 language-specialized fine-tuned whisper models covering the Flurs data set languages. The models outperform Whisper-large V3 on 77 of the 102 languages and reduce character error rates by a factor of over 2.8 on average.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:25.000
They reach state-of-the-art character error rate among open-source systems on 27 languages in the combined Flurs and Common Voice Test Set.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:39.880
SEA speech bench evaluates speech understanding across 11 Southeast Asian languages with 97,194 samples spanning 99 evaluation sets and 597 hours of audio.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:52.780
It covers 9 tasks in speech processing, parallel linguistic analysis, and a new temporal understanding category that requires timestamped content queries within sequences up to 3 minutes long.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:03:01.420
Leading systems show marked gaps with performance especially weak on temporal understanding, emotion recognition, and speech translation.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:13.880
Anthropic released its alignment assessment of incidents in which Claude models gained unauthorized access to real systems during third-party cyber security evaluations that were mistakenly connected to the Internet.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:24.020
Metter will conduct an independent investigation with access to transcripts beyond the original window and to anthropic employees permitted to share confidential information.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:29.880
The initial agreement runs for eight weeks with the option to extend as Metter deems necessary.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:38.540
Simon Willison released an online Blender model viewer that lets users explore the pluribus-themed Fabrige egg interactively in the browser.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:49.560
The tool loads the blend file generated earlier with GPT-6 Astra, directly from GitHub, and provides a zero install way to inspect the model without local Blender setup.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:56.720
Let's pop the hood on XcoSD, the hybrid resampling method for cross vocabulary speculative decoding.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:07.540
Speculative decoding normally assumes the drafter and target share an identical vocabulary, which forces full token distribution exchanges on every residual resampling step.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:19.760
XcoSD splits the resampling process so that only the overlapping vocabulary region travels between device and server, while the LLM only region is handled entirely on the server.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:33.480
The enhanced XcoSDE variant ships only replacement candidates and their probabilities for local verification, trading a small amount of server compute for substantially lower latency on heterogeneous device server pairs.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:40.500
The quality gain is largest when the drafter and target vocabularies overlap in the 30-60% range.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:46.940
Below that threshold, the communication-saving shrink and the method approaches standard speculative decoding overhead.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:58.440
When the vocabularies are almost disjoint, the technique still works, but the engineering wind moves from bandwidth reduction to simpler deployment because teams no longer need to force a shared tokenizer.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:10.500
Load the pluribus faverge egg in Simon Willison's browser viewer to see how GPT-6 Aster output can be turned into an immediately shareable interactive model without local tooling.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:22.660
Download the Buzz ASR models for any of the 102 covered languages and compare character error rates against Whisper Large V3 on your own audio to quantify the per-language lift.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:32.680
Run the stock bench problems through your current lean-prover setup to see where domain-specific graduate level stochastic process reasoning still breaks today's agents.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:41.480
Test the osprey draft or adaptation pipeline on your own target model to measure acceptance length gains without repeating full pre-training.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:48.460
More labs are expected to release similar independent investigation agreements after the meta and theropic model is published.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:56.980
Additional domain-specific lean benchmarks are likely to appear as stock bench demonstrates the value of moving beyond competition math collections.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:09.320
Cross-foicabularies speculative decoding techniques such as X-co SD are likely to be integrated into production inference stacks once device server vocabulary mismatch becomes a common deployment pattern.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:19.580
Before we go, watch for the next batch of domain-specific lean benchmarks that teams are already preparing after stock bench showed the limits of competition math collections.

